<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="title" content="🔁 Looping Crosswords" />
    <meta name="description" content="Learn about and play looping crosswords: crosswords where the fill is not bound by the edge of the grid." />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />

    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://orez-share.github.io/crosswords/looping/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="🔁 Looping Crosswords" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Learn about and play looping crosswords: crosswords where the fill is not bound by the edge of the grid." />

    <title>🔁 Looping Crosswords</title>
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="Crossword Feed" href="../feed.rss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/yellow-box.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="content">
      <h1>Looping Crosswords</h1>

      <div class="main">
        <h2 id="what">What is a Looping Crossword?</h2>
        <p>
          In a traditional crossword, each word in the grid is bounded by either a wall or the edge of the grid.
        </p>
        <p>
          A <strong>looping crossword</strong> relaxes this restriction: words will loop over the edge of the grid to the other side!
        </p>
        <!-- put an example image here -->
        <p>
          The particulars of the looping pattern are defined per-puzzle.
        </p>

        <h2 id="play">Play</h2>
        <p>
          A collection of looping crosswords I've created.
          When using the linked player you may scroll the grid by dragging&nbsp;it.
        </p>
        {{>crosswords-list}}

        <h2 id="construct">Construct</h2>
        <p>
          There is not currently a dedicated tool for creating looping crosswords.
          Please refer to <a href="format">the looping crossword format spec</a> instead.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
